.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-react - React to a message, or remove your reaction


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams react   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
React to a message with an emoji, or remove the reaction with --remove.

.PP
The reaction is sent as the reactionType string Graph documents, which is the
unicode character itself ("like" is the one named example); the CLI passes it
through, so any emoji Teams accepts works
(refs/graph/api-reference/v1.0/api/chatmessage-setreaction.md:68).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print the Graph request without sending it

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for react

.PP
\fB--remove\fP[=false]
	remove your reaction instead of adding it

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team the channel belongs to, when the reference does not say


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams(1)\fP
